BT /F1 11 Tf 50 720 Td (Page 2: Lunar Landing and Surface Operations

On July 20, 1969, Armstrong and Aldrin entered Eagle and prepared for descent to the lunar surface. Eagle landed in the Sea of Tranquility at 20:17 UTC. Neil Armstrong became the first human to step onto the lunar surface on July 21, 1969, at 02:56 UTC. Buzz Aldrin joined him 19 minutes later. Together, the astronauts spent over two hours on the surface, taking photographs and collecting 47.5 pounds of lunar rock and soil samples. Meanwhile, Michael Collins flew the Command Module Columbia alone in lunar orbit.) Tj ET
endstream
