BT /F1 11 Tf 50 720 Td (Page 3: Ascent, Earth Return, and Splashdown

After spending 21 hours and 36 minutes on the lunar surface, Eagle lifted off to rejoin Columbia in lunar orbit. After transferring samples and scientific film, Eagle was jettisoned. The astronauts began their journey back to Earth. Apollo 11 safely returned to Earth and splashed down in the Pacific Ocean on July 24, 1969, at 16:50 UTC. The crew and spacecraft were recovered by the aircraft carrier USS Hornet, and the astronauts spent 21 days in quarantine.) Tj ET
endstream
